Designed and developed an interactive Power BI dashboard to analyze nutritional and compositional trends across Starbucks' beverage menu, with a focus on calories, sugar, and caffeine content across different beverage categories. The goal of the project was to transform a raw beverage dataset into an intuitive, decision-ready visual tool that could help identify patterns in nutritional value across product lines — useful for health-conscious consumers, product teams, or menu strategy analysis.
The dashboard opens with four KPI cards summarizing the dataset at a glance: Total Beverages, Average Sugar, Average Calories, and Average Caffeine. These were built using custom DAX measures to aggregate and calculate summary statistics dynamically as filters are applied. Below the KPIs, the dashboard features five core visualizations: a line chart tracking average calories by beverage category, a donut chart showing the distribution ofbeverages across categories, a column chart comparing average caffeine levels by category, a bar chart breaking down total calories by individual beverage, and a ranked bar chart highlighting the top 5 highest-caffeine beverages on the menu.
To make the dashboard genuinely interactive rather than a static report, I added two slicers — Protein Range and Beverage Prep Method — allowing users to filter the entire view dynamically and explore how nutritional metrics shift based on preparation style or protein content. The layout was designed with a clean, branded aesthetic using Starbucks' signature green-and-cream color palette, custom iconography for each KPI card, and consistent visual hierarchy to keep the dashboard easy to scan.
